{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261114T173921Z-d30347c4", "ts": "2026-11-14T17:43:25Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.8.2-dev.1", "branch": "feature/ci-testament", "build": "01a39996ee07"}, "body": {"base_commit": "949d39eb2e8d796b18ac4dcc5afa73f5270091a5", "base_tree": "80feb843b3fc35e092b9290051926a8ab0e22651", "head_tree": "2ebabf2045481285e38fe842f8d2f9498fbdcbae", "head_commit": "01a39996ee079aab36941cf48acff20d1c32d56b", "dispatch_commit": "01a39996ee079aab36941cf48acff20d1c32d56b", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "standard", "roster": [{"role": "reviewer", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": [".github/workflows/tests.yml", ".testament.toml", "documentation/project-structure.md", "documentation/running-tests.md", "pyproject.toml", "tests/preferences/test_ci_workflow_conventions.py", "tests/test_ci_suite.py", "tools/ci-suite.py"], "files_changed": [".claude/rules/learnings/tests.md", ".github/workflows/tests.yml", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md", ".prawduct/changes/ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md", ".testament.toml", "documentation/project-structure.md", "documentation/running-tests.md", "pyproject.toml", "tests/preferences/test_ci_workflow_conventions.py", "tests/test_ci_suite.py", "tools/ci-suite.py"], "files_oracle": [".claude/rules/learnings/tests.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md", ".prawduct/changes/ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "warning", "title": "The matrix comment still tells the next person that adding a leg makes the suite prove a newer Python, which is no longer true when the pool runs the suite", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Why it broke: the change moved the suite's main run into the pool's image, and the matrix comment's earlier sentences were left as they were. In `.github/workflows/tests.yml`, the matrix comment still says 'Without the floor leg `requires-python` is a claim nothing checks. A leg for a newer release goes beside it once the suite should prove that release too.' The paragraph added under it says that a leg's interpreter now runs only the tests the pool leaves out. On the branch's own CI run (43093223235) that was 11 items; the pool ran 11430. So someone who follows the instruction and adds a 3.15 leg gets about 11 tests on 3.15 on every keyed run and believes the release is covered. The floor is now checked by the image pin (`TestThePoolImageRunsTheDeclaredFloor`), not by the leg alone. Fix: delete both sentences, or make them relational. For example: proving a newer release means a pool image on that release, because the leg runs the whole suite only when the pool did not.", "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "The test pins the pool allowance as a number but never checks the contract its comment names: that the allowance fits inside the pool job's `timeout-minutes`", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Why it broke: the test checks a value when its comment says the value feeds a downstream contract. Learnings rule: 'When a test asserts a VALUE and its comment says the value feeds a downstream contract, assert the CONTRACT'. `tests/test_ci_suite.py::test_the_allowance_is_ten_minutes` asserts `POOL_WAIT_SECONDS == 600`, and its comment says `tests.yml`'s limit for the pool job is derived from it. Nothing reads `jobs.pool.timeout-minutes` (15). Suppose someone raises the allowance to 15 minutes and updates the pin, as the test invites, but not the workflow. All tests stay green. The pool job is then killed at its time limit before it writes `suite=`, so no word reaches the next job: the pool job ends red with no verdict, and whether the `pytest` job still runs depends on how `!cancelled()` treats a timed-out job. That is the outcome the plan's 'Decisions made mid-build' says the shared allowance exists to prevent. Fix: in the conventions test, load `tools/ci-suite.py` the same way `test_ci_suite.py` does, and assert that `POOL_WAIT_SECONDS / 60` plus a stated margin for checkout, download and install is less than `jobs.pool.timeout-minutes`. Then watch it fail once with the timeout lowered to 10.", "fid": "R-2"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 2, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "The workflow and the runner agree on the `CI_SUITE_RAN_ON` name only by coincidence", "recommendation": "The conventions test checks the literal `CI_SUITE_RAN_ON` in `tests.yml`, and `test_ci_suite.py` uses the symbol `ci.RAN_ON`. If the constant were renamed in `tools/ci-suite.py`, both tests would stay green while the workflow passes a variable the runner no longer reads. The failure is safe: every keyed run would also run the whole suite on the job. But the job summary would then say 'The pool did not run the suite' when it had. Making the conventions test compare against `ci.RAN_ON` closes this. (The `suite=` output name is checked as a literal at both ends, so it does not have this problem.)", "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "running-tests.md's 'cannot use the pool' entry leaves out an error the pool itself reports, and points the reader at the key", "recommendation": "`pool_stage` treats any error the pool does not mark retryable as a refusal. That includes `population_mismatch` and an envelope-less crash, which `test_tests_the_pool_never_reported_are_named` exercises. For this case, `documentation/running-tests.md` lists only a refused key, a missing variable or a failed install, and says 'A replaced key is the usual cause'. The annotation does name the error code, so a reader can tell. Adding 'or the pool ended the run in a way the runner does not recognise (the error code says which)' would stop someone replacing a key that is fine.", "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "The new norm row is agent-originated and still waits for the owner to confirm it", "recommendation": "The `project-preferences.md` row about the key holder says 'Originated by the agent ... not ruled by the owner', and the plan's 'Decisions made mid-build' leaves it for the owner to confirm or strike. That meets the bar for being visible and vetoable, so it is not a finding. Put it to the owner as an explicit decision in the PR body, so the confirmation is recorded somewhere other than the change that created the norm.", "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "The checksum check only shows the body matches a header from the same response", "recommendation": "`fetch_cli` compares the wheel against `X-Testament-Wheel-SHA256`, which comes from the same HTTPS response. That catches a console serving bytes other than the ones it names. It does not establish authenticity beyond the TLS channel. The comment 'the digest the pool's signed release names' may lead a reader to assume a signature was verified. No change is needed if TLS to the console is the intended trust root.", "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "Records Pass and other checks: coverage", "recommendation": "Rated against the three bars: `.claude/rules/learnings/tests.md`, `.prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-ci-testament.md`, `.prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md`, `.prawduct/changes/ci-testament.md`, `.prawduct/owner-rulings.md`. None clears a bar. The governed_by dispositions (architecture, security-model, project-preferences) hold for the diff. The product check is verified: CI run 43093223235 on 6c245686 sent 11430 items to the pool, the `pytest` job got `CI_SUITE_RAN_ON: pool` and ran the 11 selected-out tests, and every job passed. No tracked file at HEAD contains either `TESTAMENT_*` repository variable's host (checked with git grep). Framework checks 7-10 do not apply: nothing under plugin/, no skill or template files.", "oid": "O-5"}], "duration_seconds": 900, "scope": "ci-testament", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": "949d39eb2e8d796b18ac4dcc5afa73f5270091a5", "record_lint": {"records": [".claude/rules/learnings/tests.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md", ".prawduct/changes/ci-testament.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md", "documentation/project-structure.md", "documentation/running-tests.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "span": "full", "bounded_from": null, "span_reason": "base-moved", "dispatched_at": "2026-11-14T17:39:25Z"}}
